-- title:
--   Presentation independence for square-presented rational local k-algebras
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field and let $C$ be a commutative local $k$-algebra, finite as a $k$-module, whose residue field is generated by $k$ in the sense that the composite $k \to \mathrm{ResidueField}(C)$ is surjective. Assume that $C$ admits a *square* presentation: there are a natural number $r$, a family $g : \mathrm{Fin}\,r \to k[y_1,\dots,y_r]$ of $r$ polynomials in $r$ variables, and an isomorphism of $k$-algebras $C \cong k[y_1,\dots,y_r]/\langle g_0,\dots,g_{r-1}\rangle$ (the ideal generated by the range of $g$). Let $N$ be a natural number, let $\psi : k[x_1,\dots,x_N] \to C$ be a surjective $k$-algebra homomorphism, and let $\mathfrak n$ be a maximal ideal of $k[x_1,\dots,x_N]$ with $\ker\psi \subseteq \mathfrak n$. Then the ideal generated by the image of $\ker\psi$ in the localisation $k[x_1,\dots,x_N]_{\mathfrak n}$ is generated by $N$ elements: there is a family $g : \mathrm{Fin}\,N \to k[x_1,\dots,x_N]_{\mathfrak n}$ with $(\ker\psi)\,k[x_1,\dots,x_N]_{\mathfrak n} = \langle \mathrm{range}\,g\rangle$. The asserted generators are elements of the localisation; they are not claimed to be images of polynomials.
--
--   This is the independence-of-presentation statement for local complete intersections over a field, in the case of a rational point: the number of relations needed locally at $\mathfrak n$ is bounded by the number of variables used, once some square presentation of $C$ exists. It is invoked by [`HopfAlgebra.exists_ker_map_localization_eq_span_of_surjective_mvPolynomial_of_isMaximal`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.exists_ker_map_localization_eq_span_of_surjective_mvPolynomial_of_isMaximal), where the complete-intersection property of a finite local algebra must be read off from an arbitrary polynomial presentation.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Algebra_exists_ker_map_localization_eq_span_of_surjective_of_exists_square_presentation_of_surjective_algebraMap_residueField.lean

